+# Why the USDC balance disappeared (and how to register it correctly)
+
+## TL;DR
+
+`useScaffoldReadContract` only knows about contracts that live in
+Scaffold-ETH's contract registry. `USDC` was never registered, so the
+hook had no address/ABI, wagmi never fired a request, and `data` sat at
+`undefined` forever — no error, no network call. The teammate pasted
+USDC into `deployedContracts.ts`, but **that file is machine-generated by
+`yarn deploy`** and gets rewritten from your on-chain deployments each
+time — so the manual entry was wiped. The correct home for a
+third-party contract like USDC is **`externalContracts.ts`**, which
+`deploy` never touches.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Why the hook returned `undefined` silently instead of erroring
+
+`useScaffoldReadContract` doesn't talk to the chain directly. It first
+resolves the contract by name, then hands off to wagmi's
+`useReadContract`. Roughly:
+
+```ts
+const { data: deployedContract } = useDeployedContractInfo(contractName); // "USDC"
+
+return useReadContract({
+  chainId: targetNetwork.id,
+  address: deployedContract?.address,   // <-- undefined when name not found
+  abi: deployedContract?.abi,           // <-- undefined when name not found
+  functionName,                          // "balanceOf"
+  args,                                  // [connectedAddress]
+  query: {
+    enabled: !Array.isArray(args) || !args.some(a => a === undefined),
+    ...
+  },
+});
+```
+
+The name lookup (`useDeployedContractInfo` → the merged
+`deployedContracts` + `externalContracts` registry, keyed by the target
+**chain id**) found no `USDC` entry for Base. So `address` and `abi`
+came back `undefined`.
+
+wagmi's `useReadContract` **treats a missing `address`/`abi` as "not
+ready" and stays idle** — it does not throw and does not send a request.
+That's the whole silent-failure story:
+
+- **No runtime error** — a missing registry entry is a normal
+  not-yet-ready state in wagmi, not an exception.
+- **No failed request in the network tab** — the query never became
+  enabled/ready, so no RPC call was ever made. There was nothing to
+  fail.
+- **`usdcBalance` stays `undefined`** — that's just the initial `data`
+  value of a query that never ran.
+
+(At most you'd get a console warning from `useDeployedContractInfo`
+about the contract not being found — nothing that surfaces in the UI.)
+
+The trap: reading a *registered* contract that reverts, or a bad RPC,
+would show an error/failed request. A *typo'd or unregistered* contract
+name looks identical to "still loading." Silence here means "I don't
+know that contract," not "the call failed."
+
+## 2. Why the teammate's fix self-destructed on deploy
+
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` is **auto-generated
+output, not a source file you edit by hand.** In the Scaffold-ETH 2
+hardhat flow, `yarn deploy` runs hardhat-deploy and then a post-deploy
+script (`generateTsAbis`) that **regenerates `deployedContracts.ts` from
+scratch** out of the `deployments/` folder (the artifacts of contracts
+*your* project actually deployed).
+
+USDC is not something your project deploys — it's Circle's contract,
+already live on Base. So it has no entry in `deployments/`. When the
+generator rewrote the file after `yarn deploy`, it emitted only your
+real deployments and the hand-pasted USDC block simply wasn't
+reproduced — it "vanished." It survived all week only because nobody
+had run `deploy` since the paste. The file has effectively a
+"do-not-edit, generated" contract; the paste was writing to a build
+artifact.
+
+## 3. The correct registration
+
+Put external/third-party contracts (ones you didn't deploy: USDC, WETH,
+a router, etc.) in:
+
+```
+packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+```
+
+This file is **hand-maintained and never overwritten by `yarn deploy`**.
+Scaffold-ETH merges it with `deployedContracts.ts`, so
+`useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC", ... })` resolves from it
+transparently — no other code changes needed.
+
+Entry for USDC on **Base mainnet (chain id `8453`)**. Native Circle USDC
+on Base is at `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913` (6 decimals):
+
+```ts
+import { GenericContractsDeclaration } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth/contract";
+
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: {
+      address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913",
+      abi: [
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "balanceOf",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [{ name: "account", type: "address" }],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint256" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "decimals",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint8" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "symbol",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "string" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "transfer",
+          stateMutability: "nonpayable",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "to", type: "address" },
+            { name: "amount", type: "uint256" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "bool" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "approve",
+          stateMutability: "nonpayable",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "spender", type: "address" },
+            { name: "amount", type: "uint256" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "bool" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "allowance",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "owner", type: "address" },
+            { name: "spender", type: "address" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint256" }],
+        },
+      ],
+    },
+  },
+} as const;
+
+export default externalContracts satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration;
+```
+
+Notes / gotchas:
+
+- **The chain-id key must match `targetNetwork`.** The registry is keyed
+  by chain id; the hook looks up under the *current* network's id. Base
+  mainnet is `8453`. If you're testing on a different network (e.g. Base
+  Sepolia `84532`, or a local fork), USDC must be registered under
+  *that* id or you're back to silent `undefined`. USDC on Base Sepolia
+  is a different (testnet) address.
+- Include (at minimum) `balanceOf`; add `decimals`/`symbol`/`transfer`/
+  `approve`/`allowance` if the payouts flow uses them. You can also just
+  drop in a full ERC-20 ABI.
+- USDC is a **proxy**, but the address above is the proxy address you
+  read against — correct for `balanceOf`. No special handling needed.
+- Remember USDC has **6 decimals**, not 18 — format the balance with
+  `formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6)`, don't reuse an 18-decimal helper.
+
+Once USDC lives in `externalContracts.ts`, the original hook works
+unchanged and survives every future `yarn deploy`.

